      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Reference inputs and output settings",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Reference to Video\nSelect an image, set the server URL and served model name, then run.\n\nConnect the optional video/audio loaders to Video References, or duplicate loaders for more inputs: up to 9 images, 3 videos, 3 audio clips, 12 total. At least one image or video is required.\n\nSlots are numbered separately per media type. Empty slots are skipped. Update prompt tags such as <Picture 1>, <Video 1>, <Audio 1> to match the connected references. Videos keep their own soundtrack in the reference upload.\n\n**Output:** 24 FPS; 124 frames (~5.17 s). Valid frame counts are 107, 124, 141, 158, 175, 192, 209, 226, 243, 260, 277, 294, 311, 328, 345.\n\n**Width x height:** 1344x768 (16:9), 1024x768 (4:3), 768x768 (1:1), 768x1024 (3:4), 768x1344 (9:16).\n\nEach reference video/audio clip must be 2\u201315 s. Total reference-video duration <=15 s; total standalone-audio duration <=15 s.\n\nRequires the expanded Video References node and the audio-preserving video output fix. See the extension README for setup and validation status."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        790,
        940
      ],
      "size": [
        480,
        455
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Optional Turbo \u2014 same workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Turbo Ref2VA\nBase mode: leave LoRA disconnected; use 50 steps, video flow shift 12, audio flow shift 3.\n\nFor the 4-step v0.1 Ref2VA Turbo adapter:\n1. Start a Ref2VA-only server with the Diffusers adapter loaded (see README).\n2. Set LoRA local_path to its path on the server, then connect LoRA to Generate Video.\n3. Set Sampling num_inference_steps to **5**; keep shifts at **12 / 3**, scale **1**.\n\nvLLM-Omni counts sigma points: 5 points give 4 denoiser evaluations. Use minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_4step_v0.1_bf16.safetensors, not the _comfyui_ export.\n\nDisconnect LoRA and restore 50 steps to return to base mode. FastH3 is a separate T2VA deployment, not this option.\n\nAdapted from the official ComfyUI MiniMax-H3 R2V workflow: https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/blob/main/templates/video_minimax_h3_r2v.json"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
